{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
We [G]left the harbour [C]early when the [G]frost was on the [D]sails
And [G]followed every [C]river past the [D]mill and through the [G]vales
The [Em]lanterns on the [C]water and the [G]barges in a [D]row
We [G]counted all the [C]milestones on the [D]long road north to [G]go
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So [C]sing it slow and [G]sing it low
And [D]keep the fire [G]burning
[C]Every mile we [G]have to go
Is a [D]mile of the road re[G]turning
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The [G]miller's daughter [C]waved to us a[G]cross the stubble [D]field
Her [G]brother at the [C]crossroads had a [D]pony and a [G]shield
We [Em]traded him a [C]fiddle for a [G]loaf of barley [D]bread
And [G]slept beneath the [C]haystacks with the [D]stars above our [G]head
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So [C]sing it slow and [G]sing it low
And [D]keep the fire [G]burning
[C]Every mile we [G]have to go
Is a [D]mile of the road re[G]turning
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Em]Oh the wind came down from the mountains and it [C]whistled through the pines, and it [G]carried every word we sang a[D]long the railway lines
[Em]Oh the snow came down on the meadow and it [C]covered all the tracks
And [G]nobody who went that way has [D]ever come back
{end_of_bridge}

