{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
At [G]last we reached the [C]border where the [G]river meets the [D]sea
The [G]gulls were on the [C]chimneys and the [D]bells rang out for [G]me
The [Em]houses had their [C]shutters closed a[G]gainst the winter [D]cold
And [G]every face that [C]greeted us was [D]weathered, kind, and [G]old
{end_of_verse}

