{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
So [C]sing it slow and [G]sing it low
And [D]keep the fire [G]burning
[C]Every mile we [G]have to go
Is a [D]mile of the road re[G]turning
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
So [G]if you hear us [C]singing when the [G]lamps are burning [D]low
Re[G]member all the [C]travellers who [D]took the road you [G]know
And [Em]raise a cup of [C]cider to the [G]ones who could not [D]stay
For [G]every road that [C]leads you north will [D]lead you home some [G]day
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Slow down on the last line and let the G ring.}
